{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Released back to `open`; the claim is withdrawn.\n\nThis ticket was claimed on a mistaken read that it carried the\n`complexity-reduction` tag. It does not — it is eval CI infrastructure\n(the `prompt-eval.yml` live arm calls `ev.run_eval` with no gate session,\nso every case errors, `run_eval` records them as unscored rather than as a\ncrash, and `continue-on-error: true` downgrades the result to an advisory\nwarning). Real defect, correctly specified, but not complexity reduction.\n\nPlan review PASSED and was certified at\n`4c4e9b2f0ba89663c9d6ac86c7297690288d6106` (job\n1793822616425741639-2dd194319b2f4ccbb56fc89773b2692b), so whoever picks this\nup next can check currency with `rebar review-plan <id> --status` instead of\npaying for a fresh review. No code was written and no worktree was created."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793823897679082113,"uuid":"0e805211-47db-491a-84c4-5d9af6f9acf9"}